From 3d26b3b0562dd00d8528dbff81c7a998904e92ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamizz <andre.tamiazzo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:55:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Record ?step= wizards as screens, keep Send link on, save
 without loading waits
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Send link: the ⋯ menu items no longer grey out when the two sides "look
like the same page". That test used the query-blind page key, so DoorDash's
?step=menu and ?step=choose-package read as one page and both items died
exactly when they were needed. Each item now shows the link it sends.

Screen params: the page key (rawDocKey / documentUrlKey) keeps the values
of step-like query params — step, stage, phase and names built on them,
plus screen. A new ?step= is a new screen on both sides, the phone is moved
to the desktop's step when a mirrored click left it behind, and the rest of
the query (modals such as ?mod=quickView, filters, tracking) still never
makes a screen. A page that writes its own first step with no click is not
a new screen.

URL changes panel (recording inspector): every URL change on either side,
which params moved, and whether it made a new screen. Params can be added
(+ tab, or typed) or dropped for the current recording only; adding one
saves the view already on screen. Every recording starts from the defaults.

Saving: loading states are no longer kept, so nothing waits for them.
Short pages are pages, not skeletons (no more 10 s wait); loading markers
and images hold a save for 2.5 s at most, a busy DOM for 3 s. A click on a
page still settling saves it right away. Loading frames are captured only
when a screen is marked Loading. The phone is not moved off a page while it
captures it. Stop saves when the page reports its last events are in
instead of after a fixed 8 s.

Rules for all of this: .claude/rules/recording.md.

