+# Recording rules
+
+How DOM Studio decides what to save while recording. Every change to capture,
+phone-twin or save logic follows these rules. If a rule has to change, change it
+here in the same commit.
+
+## Save fast — loading states are not kept
+
+- A page is saved as soon as its DOM has been still for about half a second
+  (`QUIET_LOADED_MS`). Never wait to preserve a loading or skeleton state.
+- Loading markers (spinners, skeleton or shimmer classes, `aria-busy`, image
+  slots with no source) and images still downloading hold a save for
+  `LOADING_WAIT_MAX_MS` (2.5 s) at most. A page that never goes quiet is saved
+  at `LOAD_MAX_WAIT_MS` (3 s).
+- A short page is a page. Word counts (`pageLooksLikeShell`) never hold a save;
+  they only start a background watch that replaces the card if the page fills
+  in later (`watchShellFill`).
+- A click on a page whose capture is still waiting saves it right then, before
+  the click moves the page on (`finishLoadNow`).
+- Loading frames are captured only when a screen is marked Loading
+  (`recWantsLoadingNow`). No other page pays for one.
+- Stop saves as soon as the page reports `ds-stopped` (its last events are
+  flushed). `SAVE_GRACE_MS` is only the ceiling for a page that never answers.
+
+## What makes a new screen
+
+- A screen is a page key: origin + path + hash route + screen params. The rest
+  of the query never makes a screen — modals (`?mod=quickView`), filters,
+  tracking tags.
+- Default screen params: `step`, `stage`, `phase` and names built on them
+  (`currentStep`, `onboarding_step`, `step_id`), plus `screen`.
+- The URL changes panel adds any other param (a tab, a view, even a modal) or
+  drops a default, for the current recording only. Every recording starts from
+  the defaults.
+- The page key is built in two places that must stay identical: `rawDocKey` in
+  `renderer/app.js` and `documentUrlKey` in `guest-preload.js`. Change both or
+  neither. Guests get the rules with every message that can arm them
+  (`guestScreenParams()`).
+- A page that writes its own first step with no click (lands on `/onboarding`,
+  then `?step=welcome`) is still the page being captured, not a new screen.
+
+## Desktop and phone
+
+- Both sides walk together: a click on one is mirrored on the other. If the
+  other side is left on another step of the same page (the mirrored click did
+  nothing), it follows the source's URL (`settleMirroredStep`). A side on a
+  different page may show the same state its own way (Uber's phone routes) and
+  is left where it is.
+- Never move the phone while it is capturing another screen's mobile frame. Its
+  capture queue brings it to the next page.
+- Send link (⋯ menu) is available whenever both sides are up. Never grey it out
+  on a "same page" guess.
+
+## Checking a change
+
+Run the app against a local page that moves `?step=` with `pushState`, opens a
+modal through a query param, and sends the phone to its own route. Check, on
+both sides: every step becomes one screen with its mobile frame, the modal adds
+none, the phone follows, and the time from click to saved and from Stop to
+saved.
